// TEST: Log10 Kernel Param Dimensioned (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3006
// The non-complex intrinsics are exactly {floor, ceil, log10} (mathIntrinsics
// minus complexMathIntrinsics), so all three took the pin arm and all three
// leaked a dimensioned kernel param -- not just the rounding pair. This is the
// kernel-position twin of unit-errors/007, and it reaches the SAME rejection by
// a different route: log10 has no case of its own in unitRulesForUnaryOp, so
// the OpMath catch-all's transcendental rule is what refuses it here, while
// floor/ceil (unit-errors/015) hit the dedicated scale-invariance case.
Unit meters
let D: Array<Float<meters> like Idx<3>> = [10.0, 100.0, 1000.0]
let bad = (method_for(D) <@> lambda(d) -> log10(d)) |> compute
